    "result_text": "The structured address form is in place and the full test suite passes: 18 tests, 0 failures, including both acceptance tests. I didn't add tests of my own, so the `addressLine2` composition and the update path aren't covered by any test yet.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **API contract** (`openapi.yml`): owners now accept `addressLine1` and an optional `addressLine2`. `address` is no longer marked required, so older minimal owners that send only the flat `address` are still accepted.\n- **Validation** (`RequiredOwnerFields`): an owner is valid with either a non-blank `addressLine1` or a non-blank flat `address`, plus city. If neither is supplied, `address` is still reported as missing.\n- **Normalization** (`AddressNormalizer`): two new helpers. `normalizeOptional` normalizes a field and returns nothing if it's blank. `compose` builds the address: normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` if present. Without an `addressLine1` it falls back to the normalized flat `address`.\n- **Controller**: create and update both store the normalized lines and the composed `address`, which is what responses return. So `\"10 king st\"` comes back as `addressLine1 = address = \"10 KING STREET\"`.\n- **Storage**: new `address_line1` and `address_line2` columns on the owner entity, in all four database schemas and in the JDBC repository's queries.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Household hash, postcode validation and locality:** I didn't change these. In this code they read last name, `postcode` and `city`, and nothing ever pulls a postcode out of the address text. Since `postcode` and `city` are the same fields in both forms, they already behave the same either way. The composed `address` now reflects the structured fields wherever it's read.\n- **Update now normalizes the address.** It used to store the flat address exactly as sent. This follows the spec (\"normalization applies to whichever address fields are supplied\"), but existing clients will see upper-cased, expanded addresses after an update.\n- **`addressLine2` without `addressLine1` is ignored**, and the flat `address` is used instead, because the structured form only counts when line 1 is present.",
